# BuzzQuill needs no configuration: run `npm run dev` and everything local works.
#
# Optional integrations are switched on with Vite env vars in `.env.local`
# (gitignored via the `*.local` rule) or, on Cloudflare Pages, under
# Settings → Environment variables. When a variable is unset, its feature is
# hidden and the editor runs exactly as before.
#
# ---- Google Drive (open / save files in the user's Drive) --------------------
# Both values are PUBLIC by design — they ship in the client bundle. Security is
# the `drive.file` scope (the app can only see files the user picked or it
# created) plus the restrictions you set in Google Cloud Console, not secrecy.
#
# Setup (once, in https://console.cloud.google.com):
#   1. Create a project; enable the "Google Drive API" and "Google Picker API".
#   2. OAuth consent screen: external; scope …/auth/drive.file; privacy policy
#      URL https://<your host>/privacy.html; add your domain.
#   3. Credentials → OAuth client ID (Web application). Authorized JavaScript
#      origins: https://<your host>, http://localhost:5180 (and any QA port).
#      No redirect URI is needed (token flow, popup).
#   4. Credentials → API key, restricted to HTTP referrers (your host, localhost)
#      and to the Picker API.
#
# VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=123456789012-abcdefghijklmnop.apps.googleusercontent.com
# VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=AIza...
